Package: rpi-suspend
Version: 1.5.2
Architecture: all
Maintainer: GamingTux <gamingtux@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/GamingTux/rpi-suspend
Depends: python3, systemd
Recommends: iw, rfkill
Suggests: rpi-pishutdown
Provides: rpi-fake-sleep
Replaces: rpi-fake-sleep
Conflicts: rpi-fake-sleep
Description: Universal Userspace Suspend, Standby & Clamshell Manager for Raspberry Pi
 Enables native low-power sleep, standby, and laptop clamshell mode on
 Raspberry Pi 4 / 5 & CM4 / CM5 systems where platform firmware lacks
 ACPI S3 or hardware s2idle support.
 .
 Features:
  - Seamless systemd-suspend & desktop environment integration (KDE, GNOME, Wayfire, Labwc, XFCE)
  - Cgroups v2 process freezing & single-core CPU parking (C1-C3 in hardware WFI)
  - Universal DRM DPMS & backlight blanking across Wayland and X11
  - Instant <1ms interrupt wakeup via keyboard, mouse, power button, or lid switch
  - Docked Clamshell Mode (turns off internal laptop display & keyboard when docked to an external monitor)
  - Modular hardware profile system (generic, argon-oneup, uconsole, devterm, crowview, pitop4)
  - Extensible drop-in configs (/etc/rpi-suspend.conf.d/) & hook scripts (/etc/rpi-suspend/hooks.d/)
